      <div type="clause" n="48">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 48</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="48" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="110" ed="#liebermann"/>XCII. Gif hwelc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.8-2"/> mon bið witeðeow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.9-3"/> niwan geðeowad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.10-3"/>, ⁊ hine mon betyhð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.11-3"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hæbbe ǽr geðiefed<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.12-3"/>, ær hine mon geðeowode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.13-3"/>, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> ah se teond ane swingellan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.14-3"/> æt him: bedrife hine to swingum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.15-2"/> be his ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="48" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="110" ed="#liebermann"/>XCII. Gif hwylc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.8"/> mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.4"/> biþ witeðeow niwan geþeowad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.9-2"/>, ⁊ hine mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.4"/> betyhð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.2"/>, þæt he hæbbe ær geþeofad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.10-2"/>, ær hine mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.4"/> geþeowode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.11-2"/>, þonne ah se tiond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.12-2"/> ane swingelan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.13-2"/> æt him: bedrife hine to swingum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.14-2"/> be his ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="48" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="110" ed="#liebermann"/>Be witeðeowu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mannu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Gyf hwylc mon bið wíteðeow niwan geþeowad, ⁊ hine mon betyh, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hæbbe ær geðeofad, ær hine mon geðeowade, ðonne ah se teond ane swingelan æt hím: bedrife hine to swingum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.3"/> be his ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="48" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="111" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.9"/> quis sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.10"/> wytaseruus nouiter effectus (propter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.11"/> forisfactum nouiter inseruierit), et accusetur, quod furtum fecerit, antequam in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.12"/> seruitutem transierit, tunc habeat compellens<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.13"/> uerberationem unam in eo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.14"/>: perducat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.15"/> eum ad uerbera secundum captale<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_48.lnote.oe.16"/> suum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="52" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be witeðeowum mannum.] Gif hwelc mon bið witeðeow niwan geðeowad, ⁊ hine mon betyhð<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_48.attnote.fn.2"/>, þæt he hæbbe ǽr geðiefed<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_48.attnote.fn.3"/>, ær hine mon geðeowode, þonne ah se teond ane swingellan æt him: bedrife hine to swingum<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_48.attnote.fn.4"/> be his ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="50" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="412" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XCII} Gif hwelc mon bið witeðeow niwan geðeowad, ⁊ hine mon betyhð, þæt he hæbbe ǽr geðiefed,ær hine mon geðeowode, þonne ah se teond ana swingellan æt him: bedrife hine to swingum be his ceape.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="111" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn irgendwer neuerdings<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_48.lnote.de.1"/> verknechteter Strafknecht ist, und man ihn bezichtigt, dass er bereits, bevor er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_48.lnote.de.2"/> verknechtet wurde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_48.lnote.de.3"/>, gestohlen habe, dann hat der Kläger [das Recht,] einmalige Geisselung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_48.lnote.de.4"/> an ihm [zu vollziehen]: er zwinge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_48.lnote.de.5"/> ihn zur [Erleidung der] Prügelstrafe [durch Klageeid] in Höhe seines [gestohlenen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_48.lnote.de.6"/>] Werthes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If anyone has recently been enslaved as a penalty-slave, and he is accused of having stolen before he was enslaved, then the plaintiff has [the right to inflict] one flogging on him: let him drive him to [suffer] the flogging [by an oath of accusation] to the amount of his [stolen] property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="53" ed="#attenborough"/>If any man, who has recently been reduced to penal slavery, is accused of having committed theft before he was reduced to slavery, the accuser shall have the right to scourge him once; he shall compel him to submit to a scourging by [an oath equivalent to the value of] the goods [stolen from him]<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_48.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="405" ed="#whitelock"/>If any man is a newly enslaved penal slave, and he is accused of having stolen before he was enslaved, the accuser then has the right to give him one flogging; he can compel him to the flogging by [an oath of the amount of the stolen] goods.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="413" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone has been newly reduced to the position of penal slave, and he is accused of having committed theft before he was made a slave, then the accuser has [the right] to flog him once. He shall compel him to lashings by [an oath in] the amount of his [stolen] property.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="98"><label>parallel usage (ceap)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_62">Ine 62</ref> <quote>Its sense seems more than adequately established by Ine §50 ... be his ceape ... (approximately the sense of ceape in Ine §66)</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> -glum</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to -glum</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> sit — effectus <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> propter — inseruierit <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only sit — effectus Lond; only propter — inseruierit the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">111</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">propter — furtum <hi rend="italic">überspringt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">propter — furtum omitted by R</seg></note>
