        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.10-3" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-wod <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-wod Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.11-3" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">betyh <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">betyh Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.12-3" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">geþeofad <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">geþeofad Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.13-3" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">geþeowad <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">geþeowad Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.14-3" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gelan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gelan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.oe.15-2" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">110</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-glum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-glum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Verknechtung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 9) blieb ein Jahr lang lösbar; <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> unfrei 9c. Vielleicht trat die Sippe in diesem Zeitraum noch für den des Diebstahls beschuldigten Genossen ein, während später nur der Herr die Prügel diesem Sklaven abkaufen konnte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Enslavement (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 9) remained redeemable for a year; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> unfrei 9c. Perhaps during this period the kindred still stood up for their kinsman accused of theft, whereas later only the lord could buy this slave off from the flogging</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wörtlich ‘man ihn hörig gemacht hatte’, aber anderes Subjekt als das <hi rend="italic">man</hi> zu ‘bezichtigt’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Literally ‘one had made him servile’, but with a different subject from the <hi rend="italic">man</hi> of ‘accuses’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Für Ersatz des <hi rend="spaced">während</hi> der Knechtschaft Gestohlenen haftet der Herr; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Haftung 6e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The lord is liable for making good what was stolen <hi rend="italic">during</hi> the servitude; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Haftung 6e</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Prügel 6a. 7. Der Sklave kann, weil ohne Eigentum, nicht Geldbusse oder -strafe leisten; die Leibesstrafe absorbiert jene</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Prügel 6a. 7. The slave, being without property, cannot pay compensation or a fine in money; the corporal punishment absorbs these</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gegenüber dem nicht eidesfähigen Sklaven geniesst Kläger Beweisnähe; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Against the slave, who is not competent to swear, the plaintiff enjoys the nearer right to proof; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_48.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Geburtswert des Strafknechts’ [in Frage käme nur seine Haut] versteht Price; allein diese Bed. hat <hi rend="italic">ceap</hi> nie. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Klageeid 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Price understands ‘birth-value of the penal slave’ [only his skin could come into question]; but <hi rend="italic">ceap</hi> never has this meaning. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Klageeid 10</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_48.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><label>betyhð</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">betyh</hi>. B &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_48.attnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><label>geðiefed</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">geþeofad</hi>. B, H &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_48.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><label>swingum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">swinglum</hi>. B, H &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_48.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">190</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the oath required for this purpose shall be no more than the value of the goods stolen.</seg></note>
      </div>
